{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he embraced him.</b> His compassion was stirred when he saw him bowing all those bows." "<b>And kissed him.</b> It has a dot on it; and there are those who dispute this matter in the baraita of Sifrei — some expound this dot as meaning that he did not kiss him with all his heart. Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai said: It is a known halakhah that Esau hates Jacob, but his compassion was stirred at that hour and he kissed him with all his heart (Sifrei, Numbers)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:51.920961441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}